-- Singapore Penal Code 1871 - Chapter 16 (Offences affecting the human body),
-- the part headed "Sexual offences", ss 375-377D.
--
-- Group body-b, part 2 of 2 (part 1 is pc-body-b-kidnapping.l4, ss 359-374,
-- which this module imports for the age helpers).
-- Source: Penal Code 1871, 2020 Revised Edition, SSO "Current version as at
-- 09 Sep 2026" (inputs/PC1871.txt lines 8122-10212).
--
-- What a reader must know before reading:
--
-- * ss 375, 376, 376A and 376AA are one family - penetration - and share one
--   facts record, `Sexual Penetration Facts`. They must: s 376A(1A) takes out
--   of s 376A every act that "would constitute an offence under" s 375 or
--   s 376, so s 376A's ladder reads s 375's and s 376's predicates over the
--   SAME facts. One set of facts, several charges, as cheating has ss 417/420.
-- * Each section defines AND punishes, by subsection. The charge is laid under
--   the punishing subsection: `offence under s 375(2)` / `s 375(3)`,
--   `s 376(3)` / `s 376(4)`, `s 376A(2)` / `s 376A(3)`, `s 376AA(3)`.
--   The defining subsection is named in the recital (FORK B-8).
-- * Age: the ladders read three BAND leaves (below 14; of or above 14 but below
--   16; of or above 16 but below 18), never a NOT of one of them, so that an
--   unknown age (filled FALSE by the charge generator) can never assert an
--   age band nobody supplied (PLAN s 3.4, FORK G-6). The NUMBER helpers that
--   decide each band are in pc-body-b-kidnapping.l4.
-- * s 377D(1): a reasonable mistake as to age is no defence, save under
--   s 377D(2) where 16-18 is a physical element (here: s 376AA). There is
--   accordingly no mistake-as-to-age leaf except in s 376AA's ladder.
-- * Consent is s 90's (exceptions group) as modified by s 377CB (here). The
--   ladders read one leaf, `without the victim's consent`; s 377CB is its
--   drill-down.
-- * "hurt" (s 319) and "voluntarily causes hurt" (s 321) are body-a's; the
--   aggravating leaves of ss 375(3)(a) and 376(4)(a) are joined at integration.
-- * ss 376B-377BL other than those noted, and the defences and extraterritorial
--   sections, are deferred (time); see notes/body-b-coverage.md.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pc-domain`
IMPORT `pc-general`
IMPORT `pc-body-b-kidnapping`

§ `Chapter 16 - Sexual offences`

§§ `The facts of one act of sexual penetration`

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 375, 376, 376A, 376AA, 377C, 377CA, 377D - the operative atoms, and the particulars CPC s 124 requires
DECLARE `Sexual Penetration Facts` HAS
    particulars           IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim                IS A Person      @desc The person against whom the offence was committed (B in the sections), as the charge is to name them

    -- who
    `the accused is a man`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the accused a man - a male human being (s 10), identified by sex as s 377C(3)(c) directs (identity card; sex reassignment)?
    `the victim is a woman`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the victim a woman - a female human being of any age (s 10), identified as s 377C(3)(c) directs?

    -- the acts
    `penetrates the vagina of the victim with the accused's penis`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused penetrate the victim's vagina (which includes the vulva, s 377C(1)) with his penis? (ss 375(1), 376A(1)(a), 376AA(1)(a)) - a surgically constructed part counts (s 377C(3)(b))
    `penetrates the anus or mouth of the victim with the accused's penis`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused penetrate the victim's anus or mouth with his penis? (ss 375(1A), 376A(1)(a), 376AA(1)(a))
    `sexually penetrates the vagina or anus of the victim with a part of the accused's body other than a penis, or with anything else`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused sexually (s 377C(3)(d)) penetrate the victim's vagina or anus with a part of the accused's body (not the penis, if a man), or with anything else? (ss 376(2)(a), 376A(1)(b), 376AA(1)(b))
    `causes the victim, a man, to penetrate with his penis the vagina, anus or mouth of another person including the accused`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused cause the victim, a man, to penetrate with his penis the vagina, anus or mouth of another person (who may be the accused)? (ss 376(2)(b), 376A(1)(c), 376AA(1)(c))
    `causes the victim to sexually penetrate the vagina or anus of any person with a part of the victim's body other than a penis, or with anything else`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused cause the victim to sexually penetrate the vagina or anus of any person (who may be the accused or the victim) with a part of the victim's body (not the penis, if a man), or with anything else? (ss 376(2)(c), 376A(1)(d), 376AA(1)(d))
    `the act of penetration`
                          IS A STRING  @desc The act, as the charge is to recite it after "did" - for example "penetrate the vagina of one Tan Ah Mei with your penis"

    -- consent
    `without the victim's consent`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the act done without the victim's consent? Consent is s 90's, and a consent given under a misconception of the nature or purpose of the act, or of the identity of the person doing it, is not a consent (s 377CB)

    -- age: three bands, one of which at most is TRUE
    `the victim is below 14 years of age`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the victim below 14 years of age at the time? Set from `below 14 years of age` on the victim's age. A reasonable mistake as to age is no defence (s 377D(1))
    `the victim is of or above 14 years of age but below 16 years of age`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the victim of or above 14 but below 16 years of age? Set from `of or above 14 years of age but below 16 years of age` on the victim's age (s 376A(2))
    `the victim is of or above 16 years of age but below 18 years of age`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the victim of or above 16 but below 18 years of age? Set from `of or above 16 years of age but below 18 years of age` on the victim's age (s 376AA)

    -- relationship
    `the victim is the accused's spouse`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the victim the accused's spouse (for s 375(4), his wife)? (ss 375(4), 376(5)(a), 376A(4))
    `the accused is in a relationship that is exploitative of the victim`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the accused's relationship with the victim, a minor, exploitative of the victim, as the court determines under s 377CA? (ss 375(3)(c), 376(4)(c), 376A(2)(a), 376AA(1))

    -- aggravation, ss 375(3)(a) and 376(4)(a)
    `in order to commit or to facilitate the offence, voluntarily causes hurt to any person`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc In order to commit or facilitate the offence, did the accused voluntarily cause hurt to anyone (s 321 - defined in pc-body-a; joined at integration)? (ss 375(3)(a)(i), 376(4)(a)(i))
    `in order to commit or to facilitate the offence, puts any person in fear of death or hurt`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc In order to commit or facilitate the offence, did the accused put anyone in fear of death or of hurt to that person or anyone else? (ss 375(3)(a)(ii), 376(4)(a)(ii))

    -- the accused's defences within the sections
    `proves that by reason of mistake of fact in good faith he believed that the act was done with consent`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the accused proved that, by reason of a mistake of fact in good faith (s 26B), he believed the act was done with the victim's consent? (ss 375(5), 376(5)(b); the burden is on the accused)
    `proves that by reason of mistake of fact in good faith he believed that the act against a person below 14 years of age was done with consent`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the accused proved that, by reason of a mistake of fact in good faith, he believed the act against the victim (below 14) was done with consent? (ss 375(6), 376(6) - only takes away the (3)(b) / (4)(b) punishment)
    -- s 377D(2)-(3), for s 376AA
    `reasonably and mistakenly believed that the victim was of or above 18 years of age`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused reasonably but mistakenly believe the victim was of or above 18 years of age? (s 377D(2)) - seeing the victim smoke, or admitted to a nightclub, is not a reasonable basis (s 377D Explanation)
    `took all reasonable steps to verify that the victim was of or above 18 years of age`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused take all reasonable steps to verify that the victim was of or above 18? (s 377D(3)(b)) - the same Explanation applies
    `has previously been charged in court for an offence listed in section 377D(3)(a)`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the accused previously been charged in court for an offence under s 375(1)(b), 375(1A)(b), 376(1) or 376(2) (victim below 14), 376A, 376AA, 376B, 376C, 376E-376EE, 377BG-377BL, CYPA 1993 s 8, or Women's Charter 1961 s 140(1)(i) or 145(1)? (s 377D(3)(a))

§§ `s 375 - rape`

-- 375.-(1) Any man who penetrates the vagina of a woman with his penis -
--         (a) without her consent; or
--         (b) with or without her consent, when she is below 14 years of age,
--      shall be guilty of an offence.
--      (1A) Any man (A) who penetrates, with A's penis, the anus or mouth of
--      another person (B) -
--         (a) without B's consent; or
--         (b) with or without B's consent, when B is below 14 years of age,
--      shall be guilty of an offence.
--      (4) No man shall be guilty of an offence under subsection (1)(b) or
--      (1A)(b) for an act of penetration against his wife with her consent.
--      (5) Despite section 79, no man shall be guilty of an offence under
--      subsection (1)(a) or (1A)(a) if he proves that by reason of mistake of
--      fact in good faith, he believed that the act of penetration against a
--      person was done with consent.
--
-- Limb (a) carries subsection (5); limb (b) carries subsection (4), written
-- as "not the spouse, or without consent" so that an unknown consent never
-- counts as the wife's consent (FORK B-9).
@export Paragraph (a) of section 375(1) and (1A) of the Penal Code 1871: without consent, and no proven mistake of fact in good faith as to consent (s 375(5))
GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Penetration Facts` @desc The act, the victim's consent, and the accused's proven belief
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `without consent within section 375(a)` f IF
        f's `without the victim's consent`
   ...  "Despite section 79, no man shall be guilty ... if he proves"
   ...  NOT f's `proves that by reason of mistake of fact in good faith he believed that the act was done with consent`

@export Paragraph (b) of section 375(1) and (1A) of the Penal Code 1871: below 14 years of age, with or without consent, save the wife's consent (s 375(4))
GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Penetration Facts` @desc The victim's age, and whether the victim is the accused's wife and consented
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `below 14 within section 375(b)` f IF
        "with or without consent, when"
   ...  f's `the victim is below 14 years of age`
   ...  "No man shall be guilty ... for an act of penetration against his wife with her consent"
   ...  (    NOT f's `the victim is the accused's spouse`
        OR   f's `without the victim's consent` )

@export Whether the accused commits the offence in section 375(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (rape: penile penetration of the vagina)
GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Penetration Facts` @desc The act, the victim, consent and age
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits rape within section 375(1)` f IF
        "Any"
   ...  f's `the accused is a man`
   ...  f's `penetrates the vagina of the victim with the accused's penis`
   ...  "of a"
   ...  f's `the victim is a woman`
   ...  (    `without consent within section 375(a)` f
        OR   `below 14 within section 375(b)` f )

@export Whether the accused commits the offence in section 375(1A) of the Penal Code 1871 (penile penetration of the anus or mouth)
GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Penetration Facts` @desc The act, the victim, consent and age
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits rape within section 375(1A)` f IF
        "Any"
   ...  f's `the accused is a man`
   ...  f's `penetrates the anus or mouth of the victim with the accused's penis`
   ...  (    `without consent within section 375(a)` f
        OR   `below 14 within section 375(b)` f )

@export Whether the accused commits an offence under section 375(1) or (1A) of the Penal Code 1871 (rape)
GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Penetration Facts` @desc The act, the victim, consent and age
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits rape` f IF
        `commits rape within section 375(1)` f
    OR  `commits rape within section 375(1A)` f

-- (2) Subject to subsection (3), a man who is guilty of an offence under this
--     section shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend
--     to 20 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 375(2)
`punishment prescribed by s 375(2)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "375(2)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 20 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 240
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `shall also be liable to`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

-- (3) Whoever -
--     (a) in order to commit or to facilitate the commission of an offence
--         under subsection (1) or (1A) - (i) voluntarily causes hurt to any
--         person; or (ii) puts a person in fear of death or hurt to that person
--         or any other person;
--     (b) commits an offence under subsection (1) or (1A) against a person
--         below 14 years of age without that person's consent; or
--     (c) commits an offence under subsection (1) or (1A) against a person
--         below 14 years of age with whom the offender is in a relationship that
--         is exploitative of that person,
--     shall be punished with imprisonment for a term of not less than 8 years
--     and not more than 20 years and shall also be punished with caning of not
--     less than 12 strokes.
-- (6) No man shall be punished under subsection (3)(b) if he proves that by
--     reason of mistake of fact in good faith, he believed that the act of
--     penetration against a person below 14 years of age was done with
--     consent.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 375(3)
`punishment prescribed by s 375(3)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "375(3)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term of not less than 8 years and not more than 20 years and shall also be punished with caning of not less than 12 strokes"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 240
    `minimum term in months` IS JUST 96
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `shall be punished with`
    `minimum strokes`        IS JUST 12
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 375(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (rape)
GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Penetration Facts` @desc The act, the victim, consent and age
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 375(2)` f IF
        "Subject to subsection (3), a man who is guilty of an offence under this section"
   ...  `commits rape` f

@export Whether any of the aggravating circumstances of section 375(3)(a)-(c) of the Penal Code 1871 is present
GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Penetration Facts` @desc The hurt or fear caused, the victim's age and consent, and the relationship
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `aggravated within section 375(3)` f IF
        (        "(a) in order to commit or to facilitate the commission of the offence"
            ...  (    f's `in order to commit or to facilitate the offence, voluntarily causes hurt to any person`
                 OR   f's `in order to commit or to facilitate the offence, puts any person in fear of death or hurt` ) )
    OR  (        "(b) against a person"
            ...  f's `the victim is below 14 years of age`
            ...  f's `without the victim's consent`
            ...  "(6) No man shall be punished under subsection (3)(b) if he proves"
            ...  NOT f's `proves that by reason of mistake of fact in good faith he believed that the act against a person below 14 years of age was done with consent` )
    OR  (        "(c) against a person"
            ...  f's `the victim is below 14 years of age`
            ...  f's `the accused is in a relationship that is exploitative of the victim` )

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 375(3) of the Penal Code 1871 (aggravated rape)
GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Penetration Facts` @desc The act, the victim, consent, age, and the aggravating circumstances
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 375(3)` f IF
        "Whoever ... commits an offence under subsection (1) or (1A)"
   ...  `commits rape` f
   ...  `aggravated within section 375(3)` f

§§ `s 376 - sexual assault involving penetration`

-- 376.-(1) [Deleted by Act 23 of 2021 wef 01/03/2022]
--      (2) Any person (A) who -
--         (a) sexually penetrates, with a part of A's body (other than A's
--             penis, if a man) or anything else, the vagina or anus, as the case
--             may be, of another person (B);
--         (b) causes a man (B) to penetrate, with B's penis, the vagina, anus or
--             mouth, as the case may be, of another person including A; or
--         (c) causes another person (B), to sexually penetrate, with a part of
--             B's body (other than B's penis, if a man) or anything else, the
--             vagina or anus, as the case may be, of any person including A or B,
--      shall be guilty of an offence if B did not consent to the penetration
--      or if B is below 14 years of age, whether B did or did not consent to
--      the penetration.
--      (5) No person shall be guilty of an offence under subsection (2) -
--         (a) for an act of penetration against his or her spouse with the
--             consent of that spouse; or
--         (b) if despite section 79, that person proves that by reason of
--             mistake of fact in good faith, the person believed that B
--             mentioned in those subsections did consent to the penetration and
--             B was not below 14 years of age.
@export Whether the accused commits an offence under section 376(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (sexual assault involving penetration)
GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Penetration Facts` @desc The act, the victim, consent and age
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits sexual assault by penetration within section 376(2)` f IF
        "Any person (A) who"
   ...  (    f's `sexually penetrates the vagina or anus of the victim with a part of the accused's body other than a penis, or with anything else`
        OR   f's `causes the victim, a man, to penetrate with his penis the vagina, anus or mouth of another person including the accused`
        OR   f's `causes the victim to sexually penetrate the vagina or anus of any person with a part of the victim's body other than a penis, or with anything else` )
   ...  "shall be guilty of an offence if"
   ...  (    f's `without the victim's consent`
        OR   f's `the victim is below 14 years of age` )
   ...  "(5) No person shall be guilty of an offence under subsection (2) - (a) for an act of penetration against his or her spouse with the consent of that spouse"
   ...  (    NOT f's `the victim is the accused's spouse`
        OR   f's `without the victim's consent` )
   ...  "(b) if ... that person proves that ... the person believed that B did consent to the penetration and B was not below 14 years of age"
   ...  (    NOT f's `proves that by reason of mistake of fact in good faith he believed that the act was done with consent`
        OR   f's `the victim is below 14 years of age` )

-- (3) Subject to subsection (4), a person who is guilty of an offence under
--     this section shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may
--     extend to 20 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376(3)
`punishment prescribed by s 376(3)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "376(3)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 20 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 240
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `shall also be liable to`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

-- (4) Whoever - (a) in order to commit or to facilitate ... (i) voluntarily
--     causes hurt to any person; or (ii) puts any person in fear of death or
--     hurt to himself or any other person; (b) commits an offence under
--     subsection (2) against a person below 14 years of age without that
--     person's consent; or (c) ... below 14 years of age with whom the offender
--     is in a relationship that is exploitative of that person, shall be
--     punished with imprisonment for a term of not less than 8 years and not
--     more than 20 years and shall also be punished with caning with not less
--     than 12 strokes.
-- (6) No person shall be punished under subsection (4)(b) if the person proves
--     that by reason of mistake of fact in good faith, the person believed that
--     the act of penetration against a person below 14 years of age was done
--     with consent.
--
-- The aggravating circumstances of s 376(4) are word for word those of
-- s 375(3) (with s 376(6) for s 375(6)), so one ladder serves both.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376(4)
`punishment prescribed by s 376(4)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "376(4)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term of not less than 8 years and not more than 20 years and shall also be punished with caning with not less than 12 strokes"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 240
    `minimum term in months` IS JUST 96
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `shall be punished with`
    `minimum strokes`        IS JUST 12
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 376(3) of the Penal Code 1871 (sexual assault involving penetration)
GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Penetration Facts` @desc The act, the victim, consent and age
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 376(3)` f IF
        "Subject to subsection (4), a person who is guilty of an offence under this section"
   ...  `commits sexual assault by penetration within section 376(2)` f

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 376(4) of the Penal Code 1871 (aggravated sexual assault involving penetration)
GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Penetration Facts` @desc The act, the victim, consent, age, and the aggravating circumstances
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 376(4)` f IF
        "Whoever ... commits an offence under subsection (2)"
   ...  `commits sexual assault by penetration within section 376(2)` f
   ...  `aggravated within section 375(3)` f

§§ `s 376A - sexual penetration of minor below 16 years of age`

-- 376A.-(1) Any person (A) who -
--         (a) penetrates, with A's penis, the vagina, anus or mouth, as the case
--             may be, of a person below 16 years of age (B);
--         (b) sexually penetrates, with a part of A's body (other than A's
--             penis, if a man) or anything else, the vagina or anus, as the case
--             may be, of a person below 16 years of age (B);
--         (c) causes a man below 16 years of age (B) to penetrate, with B's
--             penis, the vagina, anus or mouth, as the case may be, of another
--             person including A; or
--         (d) causes a person below 16 years of age (B) to sexually penetrate,
--             with a part of B's body (other than B's penis, if a man) or
--             anything else, the vagina or anus, as the case may be, of any
--             person including A or B,
--      shall be guilty of an offence.
--      (1A) This section does not apply to an act of penetration mentioned in
--      subsection (1) which would constitute an offence under section
--      375(1)(a), 375(1)(b) read with section 375(3), 375(1A)(a), 375(1A)(b)
--      read with section 375(3), 376(2) (if the victim B is of or above 14
--      years of age) or 376(2) (if the victim B is below 14 years of age) read
--      with section 376(4).
--      (1B) To avoid doubt - (a) it is not necessary for the prosecution to
--      prove that B did consent to an act of penetration mentioned in
--      subsection (1); and (b) it is not a defence that B did consent to that
--      act.
--      (4) No person shall be guilty of an offence under this section for an
--      act of penetration against his or her spouse with the consent of that
--      spouse.
--
-- (1B) is "for the avoidance of doubt" and adds no element: there is no consent
-- leaf in the ladder except through (1A) and (4). Inert.
@export Whether the act would constitute one of the offences under sections 375 and 376 that section 376A(1A) of the Penal Code 1871 takes out of section 376A
GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Penetration Facts` @desc The act, the victim, consent, age, and the aggravating circumstances
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `excluded from section 376A by section 376A(1A)` f IF
        (        "375(1)(a) or 375(1A)(a)"
            ...  f's `the accused is a man`
            ...  (    f's `penetrates the vagina of the victim with the accused's penis` AND f's `the victim is a woman`
                 OR   f's `penetrates the anus or mouth of the victim with the accused's penis` )
            ...  `without consent within section 375(a)` f )
    OR  (        "375(1)(b) or 375(1A)(b) read with section 375(3)"
            ...  f's `the accused is a man`
            ...  (    f's `penetrates the vagina of the victim with the accused's penis` AND f's `the victim is a woman`
                 OR   f's `penetrates the anus or mouth of the victim with the accused's penis` )
            ...  `below 14 within section 375(b)` f
            ...  `aggravated within section 375(3)` f )
    OR  (        "376(2) (if the victim B is of or above 14 years of age)"
            ...  `commits sexual assault by penetration within section 376(2)` f
            ...  NOT f's `the victim is below 14 years of age` )
    OR  (        "376(2) (if the victim B is below 14 years of age) read with section 376(4)"
            ...  `commits sexual assault by penetration within section 376(2)` f
            ...  f's `the victim is below 14 years of age`
            ...  `aggravated within section 375(3)` f )

@export Whether the accused commits an offence under section 376A(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (sexual penetration of minor below 16 years of age)
GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Penetration Facts` @desc The act, the victim's age, and whether the victim is a consenting spouse
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits sexual penetration of a minor below 16 within section 376A(1)` f IF
        "Any person (A) who"
   ...  (    f's `penetrates the vagina of the victim with the accused's penis`
        OR   f's `penetrates the anus or mouth of the victim with the accused's penis`
        OR   f's `sexually penetrates the vagina or anus of the victim with a part of the accused's body other than a penis, or with anything else`
        OR   f's `causes the victim, a man, to penetrate with his penis the vagina, anus or mouth of another person including the accused`
        OR   f's `causes the victim to sexually penetrate the vagina or anus of any person with a part of the victim's body other than a penis, or with anything else` )
   ...  "of a person below 16 years of age (B)"
   ...  (    f's `the victim is below 14 years of age`
        OR   f's `the victim is of or above 14 years of age but below 16 years of age` )
   ...  "(1A) This section does not apply to an act of penetration ... which would constitute an offence under"
   ...  NOT (`excluded from section 376A by section 376A(1A)` f)
   ...  "(4) No person shall be guilty ... against his or her spouse with the consent of that spouse"
   ...  (    NOT f's `the victim is the accused's spouse`
        OR   f's `without the victim's consent` )

-- (2) Whoever commits an offence under this section against a person (B) who
--     is of or above 14 years of age but below 16 years of age -
--     (a) in a case where the offender is in a relationship that is
--         exploitative of B, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term
--         which may extend to 20 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to
--         caning; and
--     (b) in any other case, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term
--         which may extend to 10 years, or with fine, or with both.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376A(2)(a)
`punishment prescribed by s 376A(2)(a)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "376A(2)(a)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 20 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 240
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `shall also be liable to`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376A(2)(b)
`punishment prescribed by s 376A(2)(b)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "376A(2)(b)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 120
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

-- (3) Whoever commits an offence under this section against a person (B) who
--     is below 14 years of age shall be punished with imprisonment for a term
--     which may extend to 20 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to
--     caning.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376A(3)
`punishment prescribed by s 376A(3)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "376A(3)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 20 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 240
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `shall also be liable to`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 376A(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (sexual penetration of a minor of or above 14 but below 16 years of age)
GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Penetration Facts` @desc The act, and the victim's age
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 376A(2)` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  `commits sexual penetration of a minor below 16 within section 376A(1)` f
   ...  "against a person (B) who is"
   ...  f's `the victim is of or above 14 years of age but below 16 years of age`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 376A(3) of the Penal Code 1871 (sexual penetration of a minor below 14 years of age)
GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Penetration Facts` @desc The act, and the victim's age
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 376A(3)` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  `commits sexual penetration of a minor below 16 within section 376A(1)` f
   ...  "against a person (B) who is"
   ...  f's `the victim is below 14 years of age`

§§ `s 376AA - exploitative sexual penetration of minor of or above 16 but below 18 years of age`

-- 376AA.-(1) Any person (A) who is in a relationship that is exploitative of a
--      person of or above 16 years of age but below 18 years of age (B) shall
--      be guilty of an offence if A -
--         (a) penetrates, with A's penis, if A is a man, the vagina, anus or
--             mouth, as the case may be, of B;
--         (b) sexually penetrates, with a part of A's body (other than A's
--             penis, if A is a man) or anything else, the vagina or anus, as the
--             case may be, of B;
--         (c) causes B, if a man, to penetrate, with B's penis, the vagina, anus
--             or mouth, as the case may be, of another person including A; or
--         (d) causes B to sexually penetrate, with a part of B's body (other
--             than B's penis, if B is a man) or anything else, the vagina or
--             anus, as the case may be, of any person including A or B.
--      (2) For the purposes of subsection (1) - (a) it is not necessary for the
--      prosecution to prove that B did or did not consent to the act mentioned
--      in that subsection; and (b) to avoid doubt, it is not a defence that B
--      did consent to that act.
--      (3) ... imprisonment for a term which may extend to 15 years, and shall
--      also be liable to fine or to caning.
--
-- s 377D(2)-(3) gives a defence of reasonable mistaken belief that the minor
-- was of or above 18, because "of or above 16 but below 18" is a physical
-- element here; it is in the ladder, as the defence's own section says when it
-- is available.
@export Whether the defence of reasonable mistaken belief as to age in section 377D(2) of the Penal Code 1871 is available and made out
GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Penetration Facts` @desc The accused's belief as to age, the steps taken to verify it, and any previous charge
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `defence of mistaken belief as to age within section 377D(2)` f IF
        f's `reasonably and mistakenly believed that the victim was of or above 18 years of age`
   ...  "(3) the defence ... is no longer available if ... the person charged ... (b) failed to take all reasonable steps to verify"
   ...  f's `took all reasonable steps to verify that the victim was of or above 18 years of age`
   ...  "(a) has previously been charged in court for an offence under"
   ...  NOT f's `has previously been charged in court for an offence listed in section 377D(3)(a)`

@export Whether the accused commits an offence under section 376AA(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (exploitative sexual penetration of minor of or above 16 but below 18 years of age)
GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Penetration Facts` @desc The relationship, the victim's age, and the act
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits exploitative sexual penetration of a minor within section 376AA(1)` f IF
        "Any person (A) who is"
   ...  f's `the accused is in a relationship that is exploitative of the victim`
   ...  "of a person"
   ...  f's `the victim is of or above 16 years of age but below 18 years of age`
   ...  "shall be guilty of an offence if A"
   ...  (    (    f's `penetrates the vagina of the victim with the accused's penis`
              OR  f's `penetrates the anus or mouth of the victim with the accused's penis` )
         AND f's `the accused is a man`
        OR   f's `sexually penetrates the vagina or anus of the victim with a part of the accused's body other than a penis, or with anything else`
        OR   f's `causes the victim, a man, to penetrate with his penis the vagina, anus or mouth of another person including the accused`
        OR   f's `causes the victim to sexually penetrate the vagina or anus of any person with a part of the victim's body other than a penis, or with anything else` )
   ...  "section 377D(2):"
   ...  NOT (`defence of mistaken belief as to age within section 377D(2)` f)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 376AA(3)
`punishment prescribed by s 376AA(3)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "376AA(3)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 15 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 180
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `shall also be liable to`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 376AA(3) of the Penal Code 1871 (exploitative sexual penetration of minor of or above 16 but below 18 years of age)
GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Penetration Facts` @desc The relationship, the victim's age, and the act
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 376AA(3)` f IF
        "A person who is guilty of an offence under this section"
   ...  `commits exploitative sexual penetration of a minor within section 376AA(1)` f

§§ `The penetration charges`

GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Penetration Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the said victim` f MEANS CONCAT "the said ", f's victim's name

GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Penetration Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the age clause` f MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF f's `the victim is below 14 years of age`
        THEN CONCAT ", ", `the said victim` f, " then being below 14 years of age"
        IF f's `the victim is of or above 14 years of age but below 16 years of age`
        THEN CONCAT ", ", `the said victim` f, " then being of or above 14 years of age but below 16 years of age"
        IF f's `the victim is of or above 16 years of age but below 18 years of age`
        THEN CONCAT ", ", `the said victim` f, " then being of or above 16 years of age but below 18 years of age"
        OTHERWISE ""

GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Penetration Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the consent clause` f MEANS
    IF   f's `without the victim's consent`
    THEN CONCAT ", without ", (`possessive pronoun` (f's victim's pronoun)), " consent"
    ELSE ""

GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Penetration Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the aggravation clause` f MEANS
    `joined with` "" (concat (LIST
        (`included if` (f's `in order to commit or to facilitate the offence, voluntarily causes hurt to any person`) ", and in order to commit the said offence, did voluntarily cause hurt"),
        (`included if` (f's `in order to commit or to facilitate the offence, puts any person in fear of death or hurt`) ", and in order to commit the said offence, did put a person in fear of death or hurt"),
        (`included if` (f's `the victim is below 14 years of age` AND f's `the accused is in a relationship that is exploitative of the victim`) ", being in a relationship that is exploitative of the said person")))

GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Penetration Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the recital of the penetration` f MEANS
    CONCAT "did ", f's `the act of penetration`, `the age clause` f, `the consent clause` f

GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Penetration Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of rape not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `the accused is a man`) "any man"),
        (`missing unless` ((f's `penetrates the vagina of the victim with the accused's penis` AND f's `the victim is a woman`) OR f's `penetrates the anus or mouth of the victim with the accused's penis`) "penetrates the vagina of a woman, or the anus or mouth of another person, with his penis"),
        (`missing unless` (`without consent within section 375(a)` f OR `below 14 within section 375(b)` f) "(a) without consent, or (b) with or without consent when below 14 years of age"),
        (`missing unless` (`commits rape` f) "the elements of section 375(1) or (1A) taken together"))

@export Frame a charge under section 375(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (rape), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Penetration Facts` @desc The act, the victim, consent, age, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 375(2)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "375(2)" "rape"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 375(2)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 375(2)` f)
        (`the recital of the penetration` f)
        (`elements of rape not made out` f)

@export Frame a charge under section 375(3) of the Penal Code 1871 (aggravated rape), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Penetration Facts` @desc The act, the victim, consent, age, the aggravating circumstances, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 375(3)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "375(3)" "rape"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 375(3)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 375(3)` f)
        (CONCAT (`the recital of the penetration` f), `the aggravation clause` f)
        (concat (LIST (`elements of rape not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (`aggravated within section 375(3)` f) "(a) voluntarily causes hurt, or puts a person in fear of death or hurt, in order to commit or facilitate the offence; (b) against a person below 14 years of age without consent; or (c) against a person below 14 years of age in an exploitative relationship")))

GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Penetration Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of sexual assault by penetration not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `sexually penetrates the vagina or anus of the victim with a part of the accused's body other than a penis, or with anything else`
                           OR f's `causes the victim, a man, to penetrate with his penis the vagina, anus or mouth of another person including the accused`
                           OR f's `causes the victim to sexually penetrate the vagina or anus of any person with a part of the victim's body other than a penis, or with anything else`)
            "sexually penetrates (other than with the penis), or causes B to penetrate, as section 376(2)(a)-(c) describes"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `without the victim's consent` OR f's `the victim is below 14 years of age`) "B did not consent to the penetration, or B is below 14 years of age"),
        (`missing unless` (`commits sexual assault by penetration within section 376(2)` f) "the elements of section 376(2) taken together, and no answer under section 376(5)"))

@export Frame a charge under section 376(3) of the Penal Code 1871 (sexual assault involving penetration), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Penetration Facts` @desc The act, the victim, consent, age, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 376(3)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "376(3)" "sexual assault involving penetration"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 376(3)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 376(3)` f)
        (`the recital of the penetration` f)
        (`elements of sexual assault by penetration not made out` f)

@export Frame a charge under section 376(4) of the Penal Code 1871 (aggravated sexual assault involving penetration), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Penetration Facts` @desc The act, the victim, consent, age, the aggravating circumstances, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 376(4)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "376(4)" "sexual assault involving penetration"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 376(4)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 376(4)` f)
        (CONCAT (`the recital of the penetration` f), `the aggravation clause` f)
        (concat (LIST (`elements of sexual assault by penetration not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (`aggravated within section 375(3)` f) "(a) voluntarily causes hurt, or puts a person in fear of death or hurt, in order to commit or facilitate the offence; (b) against a person below 14 years of age without consent; or (c) against a person below 14 years of age in an exploitative relationship")))

GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Penetration Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of sexual penetration of a minor not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `penetrates the vagina of the victim with the accused's penis`
                           OR f's `penetrates the anus or mouth of the victim with the accused's penis`
                           OR f's `sexually penetrates the vagina or anus of the victim with a part of the accused's body other than a penis, or with anything else`
                           OR f's `causes the victim, a man, to penetrate with his penis the vagina, anus or mouth of another person including the accused`
                           OR f's `causes the victim to sexually penetrate the vagina or anus of any person with a part of the victim's body other than a penis, or with anything else`)
            "an act of penetration within section 376A(1)(a)-(d)"),
        (`missing unless` (NOT (`excluded from section 376A by section 376A(1A)` f)) "the act is not one that would constitute an offence under section 375 or 376 excluded by section 376A(1A)"),
        (`missing unless` (`commits sexual penetration of a minor below 16 within section 376A(1)` f) "the elements of section 376A(1) taken together"))

@export Frame a charge under section 376A(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (sexual penetration of minor of or above 14 but below 16 years of age), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Penetration Facts` @desc The act, the victim's age, the relationship, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 376A(2)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "376A(2)" "sexual penetration of minor below 16 years of age"
        (IF f's `the accused is in a relationship that is exploitative of the victim`
         THEN `punishment prescribed by s 376A(2)(a)`'s words
         ELSE `punishment prescribed by s 376A(2)(b)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 376A(2)` f)
        (`the recital of the penetration` f)
        (concat (LIST (`elements of sexual penetration of a minor not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `the victim is of or above 14 years of age but below 16 years of age`) "B is of or above 14 years of age but below 16 years of age")))

@export Frame a charge under section 376A(3) of the Penal Code 1871 (sexual penetration of minor below 14 years of age), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Penetration Facts` @desc The act, the victim's age, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 376A(3)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "376A(3)" "sexual penetration of minor below 16 years of age"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 376A(3)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 376A(3)` f)
        (`the recital of the penetration` f)
        (concat (LIST (`elements of sexual penetration of a minor not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `the victim is below 14 years of age`) "B is below 14 years of age")))

@export Frame a charge under section 376AA(3) of the Penal Code 1871 (exploitative sexual penetration of minor of or above 16 but below 18 years of age), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Sexual Penetration Facts` @desc The relationship, the victim's age, the act, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 376AA(3)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "376AA(3)" "exploitative sexual penetration of minor of or above 16 but below 18 years of age"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 376AA(3)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 376AA(3)` f)
        (CONCAT (`the recital of the penetration` f), ", being in a relationship that is exploitative of ", `the said victim` f)
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `the accused is in a relationship that is exploitative of the victim`) "in a relationship that is exploitative of B"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `the victim is of or above 16 years of age but below 18 years of age`) "B is of or above 16 years of age but below 18 years of age"),
            (`missing unless` (NOT (`defence of mistaken belief as to age within section 377D(2)` f)) "no defence of reasonable mistaken belief that B was of or above 18 years of age (section 377D(2))"),
            (`missing unless` (`commits exploitative sexual penetration of a minor within section 376AA(1)` f) "the elements of section 376AA(1) taken together")))

§§ `s 377BA - word or gesture intended to insult modesty of any person`

-- 377BA. Whoever, intending to insult the modesty of any person, utters any
--        word, makes any sound or gesture, or exhibits any object, intending
--        that such word or sound will be heard, or that such gesture or object
--        will be seen by such person, or intrudes upon the privacy of such
--        person, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may
--        extend to one year, or with fine, or with both.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BA - the operative atoms, and the particulars CPC s 124 requires
DECLARE `Insult to Modesty Facts` HAS
    particulars           IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim                IS A Person      @desc The person whose modesty was to be insulted, as the charge is to name them
    `intending to insult the modesty of any person`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend to insult the modesty of the victim? (s 377BA - a fault element)
    `utters any word`     IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused utter any word? (s 377BA)
    `makes any sound`     IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused make any sound? (s 377BA)
    `makes any gesture`   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused make any gesture? (s 377BA)
    `exhibits any object` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused exhibit any object? (s 377BA)
    `intending that such word or sound will be heard, or that such gesture or object will be seen, by such person`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend the victim to hear the word or sound, or to see the gesture or object? (s 377BA)
    `intrudes upon the privacy of such person`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intrude upon the victim's privacy? (s 377BA)
    `what was said, done or exhibited`
                          IS A STRING  @desc What the accused said, did, exhibited or how the accused intruded, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "by uttering the words 'come and sit on my lap'"

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 377BA of the Penal Code 1871 (word or gesture intended to insult modesty of any person)
GIVEN f IS A `Insult to Modesty Facts` @desc The words, sounds, gestures, objects or intrusion, and the intent
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 377BA` f IF
        "Whoever,"
   ...  f's `intending to insult the modesty of any person`
   ...  (    (    (    f's `utters any word`
                  OR   f's `makes any sound`
                  OR   f's `makes any gesture`
                  OR   f's `exhibits any object` )
             AND  f's `intending that such word or sound will be heard, or that such gesture or object will be seen, by such person` )
        OR   f's `intrudes upon the privacy of such person` )

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377BA
`punishment prescribed by s 377BA` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "377BA"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to one year, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 12
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Frame a charge under section 377BA of the Penal Code 1871 (word or gesture intended to insult modesty of any person), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Insult to Modesty Facts` @desc The words, sounds, gestures, objects or intrusion, the intent, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 377BA` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "377BA" "word or gesture intended to insult modesty of any person"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 377BA`'s words)
        (`offence under s 377BA` f)
        (CONCAT "did, intending to insult the modesty of ", (`one person` (f's victim)), ", ",
                (IF f's `intrudes upon the privacy of such person`
                 THEN CONCAT "intrude upon the privacy of the said ", f's victim's name
                 ELSE CONCAT "utter words, make sounds or gestures, or exhibit an object, intending that they be heard or seen by the said ", f's victim's name),
                ", to wit, ", f's `what was said, done or exhibited`)
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `intending to insult the modesty of any person`) "intending to insult the modesty of any person"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `utters any word` OR f's `makes any sound` OR f's `makes any gesture` OR f's `exhibits any object` OR f's `intrudes upon the privacy of such person`) "utters any word, makes any sound or gesture, exhibits any object, or intrudes upon the privacy of such person"),
            (`missing unless` (`offence under s 377BA` f) "the elements of section 377BA taken together")))

§§ `s 377CA - meaning of exploitative relationship`

-- 377CA.-(1) ... whether an accused person's relationship with a person below
--      18 years of age (called in this section a minor) is exploitative of the
--      minor is to be determined by the court in the circumstances of each
--      case and the court must have regard to [(a) age, (b) age difference,
--      (c) nature of the relationship, (d) degree of control or influence].
--      (2) ... it is presumed until the contrary is proved that an accused
--      person's relationship with a minor is exploitative where the
--      relationship is any of the following: (a)-(g) ...
--      (3) The presumption in subsection (2) does not apply to a person who is
--      lawfully married to a minor ...
--
-- Subsection (1) is a judgement for the court on four factors, not a rule the
-- encoding can decide: the ladders read its outcome as the leaf
-- `the accused is in a relationship that is exploitative of the victim`.
-- Subsections (2)-(3) are a presumption, encoded as a drill-down on its own
-- record, with the rebuttal as a leaf.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377CA(2)-(3) - the relationships presumed exploitative
DECLARE `Exploitative Relationship Facts` HAS
    `the accused is the parent, step-parent, guardian or foster parent of the minor`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (a) Is the accused the minor's parent, step-parent, guardian or foster parent?
    `the accused is the de facto partner of the parent, guardian or foster parent of the minor`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (b) Is the accused the de facto partner of the minor's parent, guardian or foster parent?
    `the accused is a member of the teaching or management staff of the minor's school or educational institution`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (c) Is the accused on the teaching or management staff of the school or educational institution where the minor is a student?
    `the accused has an established personal relationship with the minor in connection with religious, sporting, musical or other instruction`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (d) Does the accused have an established personal relationship with the minor in connection with religious, sporting, musical or other instruction to the minor?
    `the accused is a custodial officer of an institution in which the minor is detained`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (e) Is the accused a custodial officer of an institution where the minor is detained?
    `the accused is a registered medical practitioner, registered TCM practitioner or psychologist and the minor is a patient`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (f) Is the accused a registered medical practitioner, registered traditional Chinese medicine practitioner or psychologist, and the minor a patient of the accused?
    `the accused is an advocate and solicitor or a counsellor and the minor is a client`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (g) Is the accused an advocate and solicitor or a counsellor, and the minor a client of the accused?
    `the accused is lawfully married to the minor`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the accused lawfully married to the minor? (s 377CA(3))
    `the contrary is proved`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the accused proved that the relationship is not exploitative, displacing the presumption? (s 377CA(2) "until the contrary is proved")

@export Whether a relationship with a minor is presumed exploitative under section 377CA(2)-(3) of the Penal Code 1871, and the presumption stands
GIVEN r IS A `Exploitative Relationship Facts` @desc The relationship between the accused and the minor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `presumed exploitative within section 377CA(2)` r IF
        "it is presumed until the contrary is proved that an accused person's relationship with a minor is exploitative where the relationship is any of the following:"
   ...  (    r's `the accused is the parent, step-parent, guardian or foster parent of the minor`
        OR   r's `the accused is the de facto partner of the parent, guardian or foster parent of the minor`
        OR   r's `the accused is a member of the teaching or management staff of the minor's school or educational institution`
        OR   r's `the accused has an established personal relationship with the minor in connection with religious, sporting, musical or other instruction`
        OR   r's `the accused is a custodial officer of an institution in which the minor is detained`
        OR   r's `the accused is a registered medical practitioner, registered TCM practitioner or psychologist and the minor is a patient`
        OR   r's `the accused is an advocate and solicitor or a counsellor and the minor is a client` )
   ...  "(3) The presumption ... does not apply to a person who is lawfully married to a minor"
   ...  NOT r's `the accused is lawfully married to the minor`
   ...  "until the contrary is proved"
   ...  NOT r's `the contrary is proved`

§§ `s 377CB - consent given under misconception in sexual offences`

-- 377CB.-(1) Despite section 90(a)(ii), a consent for the purposes of an act
--      which is the physical element of a sexual offence is not a consent given
--      by a person under a misconception of fact only if it is directly related
--      to - (a) the nature of the act, namely that it is not of a sexual
--      nature; (b) the purpose of the act, namely that it is not for a sexual
--      purpose; or (c) the identity of the person doing the act, and the person
--      doing the act knows, or has reason to believe, that the consent was
--      given in consequence of such misconception.
--
-- This is the drill-down for the `without the victim's consent` leaf, where the
-- apparent consent was procured by a misconception. The rest of s 90 is the
-- exceptions group's.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 377CB(1)
DECLARE `Misconception Facts` HAS
    `the victim consented under a misconception of fact`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the victim give an apparent consent under a misconception of fact?
    `the misconception is that the act is not of a sexual nature`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (a) Was the misconception directly related to the nature of the act - that it was not sexual?
    `the misconception is that the act is not for a sexual purpose`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (b) Was it directly related to the purpose of the act - that it was not for a sexual purpose?
    `the misconception is as to the identity of the person doing the act`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (c) Was it directly related to the identity of the person doing the act - not merely that person's attributes (Illustration (d))?
    `the person doing the act knows or has reason to believe that the consent was given in consequence of the misconception`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused know, or have reason to believe (s 26), that the consent was given because of that misconception?

@export Whether an apparent consent to the physical element of a sexual offence is "not a consent" by reason of misconception within section 377CB of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN m IS A `Misconception Facts` @desc The misconception, what it related to, and what the accused knew
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `not a consent within section 377CB` m IF
        m's `the victim consented under a misconception of fact`
   ...  "only if it is directly related to"
   ...  (    m's `the misconception is that the act is not of a sexual nature`
        OR   m's `the misconception is that the act is not for a sexual purpose`
        OR   m's `the misconception is as to the identity of the person doing the act` )
   ...  "and"
   ...  m's `the person doing the act knows or has reason to believe that the consent was given in consequence of the misconception`

-- s 377A. [Repealed by Act 39 of 2022 wef 03/01/2023]
